# Production build & VPS deploy (Ittefaq POS)

## VPS / ports — do not disturb existing setup

- **Hostinger VPS** keeps its own nginx, PM2, ports, and `.env`. Repo changes must not force new ports or replace server configs.
- Deploy on VPS: **`git pull` → `npm ci` → `npm run build` → `pm2 restart`** (existing process name from `pm2 list`).

## Environments

| | Command | Where |
|--|---------|--------|
| Develop | `npm run dev` | PC, port 3000, real `.env` DB |
| Test production build locally | `npm run build` then `npm run start` | PC, port 3000 |
| Live users | `npm run build` + PM2 **`next start`** | Hostinger — same as before |

## Build

- `npm run build` → `prisma generate` (or `npm run generate:safe` on Windows if DLL locked) + **`next build --webpack`**.
- Do not switch to Turbopack-only without `WebSdk` alias.

## Client bootstrap (do not regress)

- **`chunk-error-recovery.js`**: max **2** auto-reloads; no infinite reload loop.
- **`use-login.js`**: full navigation after login (`window.location.assign`).

## Pre-push

1. `npm run build` succeeds on your PC.
2. Push only app code from the repo (no local-only server configs).
